From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:24:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: mailbox: keep the send wait killable, not
 interruptible

The 7.3 port dropped one hunk of 460a6e77f0 ("soc: apple: mailbox: add
the secure RTBuddy port and sleep helpers", 1.617): the send loop's wait
for FIFO space went back to wait_for_completion_interruptible_timeout().

The freezer wakes every task it freezes with a fake signal. A sender
that is waiting for FIFO space when a system sleep starts then returns
-ERESTARTSYS from apple_mbox_send() in the middle of a coprocessor
exchange, and a message half sent can break that handshake (RTKit, PMP,
SEP, DCP all send through here). 1.617 waited killably: only a fatal
signal ends the wait early, the deadline still bounds it, and the
"t < 0" path is unchanged.

Restore the 1.617 wait. Nothing else of 460a6e77f0 is missing on 7.3
(send_ready, set_recv_enabled, the ASCWrap v6 helpers and the secure
RTBuddy port are all present).

Fixes: 5bc1f31f98 ("j604: integrate the J604 series onto Aurora 7.3 (shipping snapshot)")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c b/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c
index ba02c90cdb..5de19159a3 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c
@@ -757,7 +757,8 @@ int apple_mbox_send(struct apple_mbox *mbox, const struct apple_mbox_msg msg,
 		 * it unmasked for them. The handler masks it when it fires,
 		 * and removal masks it otherwise.
 		 */
-		t = wait_for_completion_interruptible_timeout(
+		/* Not for the freezer's signal: a message half sent can break a handshake. */
+		t = wait_for_completion_killable_timeout(
 			&mbox->tx_empty,
 			min(remaining, msecs_to_jiffies(APPLE_MBOX_TX_RECHECK_MS)));
 		if (t < 0)
